schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-REDESIGN
wu: E-REDESIGN.W4
tests:
  unit:
    count: 18
    covers: |
      ui/src/FlowList.test.tsx — 15 tests, a NEW FILE: this screen was the only one in ui/src/ with no adjacent test, which the epic plan names as a row to close. Each test asserts what the design DECLARES, not that the component renders. Cells: the verb carries its tone class (GET→text-ok, DELETE→text-warn, POST→text-create), the time is an absolute HH:MM:SS clock rather than a relative phrase, the status pill's accessible name carries its reason phrase ("200 OK"), and a pending flow's DurationText renders the invisible fixed-width placeholder (text-transparent, aria-hidden) rather than collapsing the column. Absences: no flows + no filter says "no flows yet" and names the proxy address AND asserts the filter sentence is ABSENT; no flows + a filter says "no flows match this filter" and asserts "no flows yet" is ABSENT — the two are checked against each other, because one message serving both causes is the exact defect the design's Tune T3 removed. Keyboard: the region is one tab stop with aria-activedescendant pointing at the selected row's id; ArrowDown and ArrowUp each move by one; NEITHER WRAPS at its end (both ends tested separately); either arrow into an unselected list lands on the first row (the design's stated Select convention, both directions tested); Enter and Space each open; the pointer path still works. Truncation, on the record: host and path carry truncate AND the row carries the full path as its title — both halves asserted, so a later well-meaning "fix" that drops the title fails rather than passes. Windowing: a 200-row list is driven past the rendered window and the virtualizer is asserted to be ASKED to follow at every step, including steps past the window's edge — see the note field for what jsdom can and cannot prove here.
      ui/src/flow.test.ts — updated to FlowRow's reduced shape. toRow now returns exactly {host, path}, asserted by key set, because the four other values must reach TimestampText / MethodLabel / StatusPill / DurationText raw — every one of those components' @avoid forbids caller-side pre-formatting.
      ui/src/App.test.tsx — the flow count renders through TonedText at muted (text-ink-mute + font-mono), which is Tune T2: a bare span read as a label, a TonedText reads as a value with a deliberately absent tone.
  integration:
    count: 3
    covers: "ui/src/App.test.tsx — the bounded contract is the screen against a live API, which App.test.tsx already exercises over a fake TrawlerApi. Three paths cross the App/FlowList seam and live in neither file alone: (1) a proven launch with no traffic renders the nothing-captured absence and NOT the filter one; (2) a host filter that matches nothing renders the filter absence and NOT the launch one — extending an existing test that previously asserted only that some empty state appeared, which could not tell the two apart; (3) the keyboard alone (ArrowDown ×2, Enter) selects the second row and opens its detail, asserted by api.getFlow being called with f2 — the seam matters because FlowList owns the keys and App owns the selection state and the detail fetch."
  e2e:
    count: 16
    covers: "cargo xtask ui e2e — 16/16 specs, 2 files. NOT waived: this WU changes rendered screens. A NEW UC-4 block (6 specs) implements the epic e2e plan's UC-4 row against the real WebKit window: a proxied request lands as a row carrying an absolute time, a toned verb and a duration; the status pill carries its reason phrase in its accessible name; a filter narrows the list; an unmatched filter shows the filter absence and NOT the launch one; clearing it restores the rows; and the keyboard alone selects a row and opens its detail — focused via browser.execute rather than a click, so the assertion is about the keys and not a pointer. UC-5's existing block (6 specs) and onboarding.spec.ts (4 specs) stay green unchanged, which is exactly why they could not have been this WU's proof: they assert on data-testids this WU deliberately preserved."
verified:
  - "cd ui && pnpm test — 545 passed, 43 files, 0 failed (527 before this WU; +15 FlowList.test.tsx, +3 App.test.tsx)."
  - "cargo xtask ui e2e — 16/16 across 2 spec files, against the real Tauri/WebKit window and an ephemeral core."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src — silent. The closed-vocabulary lint (DEC-17) is the check that text-center and flex-wrap are declared scale members and not classes that resolve to nothing."
  - "npx tsc -b — clean over FlowRow's reduced shape and the new filtered prop."
  - "cargo test && cargo xtask gate0 — green. No Rust changed; re-walked because the gate does."
  - "cargo xtask design-scope epic/redesign HEAD — three rendered files (App.tsx, FlowList.tsx, Layout.tsx), all three cited on the cr/v3 note. ui/src/flow.ts is NOT listed: it renders nothing, so it owes no citation."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc on both docs/work/2026-09-05-redesign-w4-plan.html and -w4-result.html — green."
note: "THE E2E ASSERTIONS ARE THE ONES THAT MATTER, because each one FAILS AGAINST THE PRE-WU BUILD: the reason phrase in the pill's accessible name, the filter absence's own sentence, and a keyboard path that did not exist at all (the row was a div with an onClick, carrying aria-selected on nothing). A UC-4 block written against the testids this screen already had would have passed green while proving nothing, which is the trap the epic plan names when it says the preserved testids cannot be the epic's proof on their own. WHAT THE UNIT LAYER CANNOT PROVE, stated rather than implied: jsdom implements no scrollTo, and the virtualizer's scroll-into-view is exactly a scrollElement.scrollTo call — so under jsdom the rendered window PROVABLY cannot follow a selection. The 200-row test therefore asserts the virtualizer is ASKED at every step including past the window's edge, and its comment says so; that the browser then honours the request is the e2e's assertion, not this one. This gap was a REVIEW FINDING, not a designed choice: every keyboard test originally used a 3-row fixture that fits the mocked 600px viewport whole, so the virtualizer never windowed and the scroll-into-view mechanism — which exists precisely so the keyboard path is not nominal — could have been deleted with the suite green. TWO OTHER REVIEW FINDINGS were also real and fixed: the empty state hardcoded 127.0.0.1:7420 where api.ts's own comment forbids it in as many words (DEC-12, 'configurable, never hardcoded in component code'), so under VITE_TRAWLER_PROXY the list and onboarding would have named different addresses — the test now asserts against defaultProxyAddr() rather than a literal, so it cannot re-freeze; and the design's wire-markup line asks for data-wire on all six payload cells plus data-wire=collection/data-order on the region and data-wire=none on the header chrome, of which only two cells had it. THE TRUNCATION IS DELIBERATE AND TESTED AS SUCH: host and path truncate because a virtualized fixed-height row cannot wrap, which W3 recorded as a narrow violation of wrap-not-truncate paid for by the row's title and the detail pane, and escalated to W11 because the rulebook has no clause for this case. The rulebook is unmoved (aeff5b0), so nothing about that verdict changed here."
